WEBVTT

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:10.940
<i>Spring! On this day, Teiai is conducting...</i>

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:16.390
<i>its annual round of hiring interviews!</i>

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:22.470
<i>To start working at Teiai, 
before anything else,</i>

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:27.480
Teiai Financial Corporation Human Resources Division
6-12-X Toranomon, Minato-ku, Tokyo

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.480
<i>you need to submit an entry sheet!</i>

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:29.840
<i>And it needs to be sent in...</i>

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.700
<i>before the deadline!</i>

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.720
<i>Then you just wait.</i>

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.720
The famous comedy duo
everyone's talking about!

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.720
After the break!
A string of shocking answers leaves the studio in shock...!

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:36.910
<i>Until you're notified as to whether 
or not you'll get an interview,</i>

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:37.890
<i>you're on standby!</i>

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:43.390
<i>If you receive a notice that you 
were accepted within a few days,</i>

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:46.020
<i>you take the written exam, 
and at long last,</i>

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.400
<i>you set foot in Teiai <i>Finance</i>...</i>

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.610
<i>for the interview itself.</i>

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.650
Teiai Finance
Interview Location

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:52.650
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.410
I see we have some again this year.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:04.360
A few people who should have 
a clue about TPO, but don't.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:07.430
What do you mean, sir?

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:14.300
The interview's already begun.

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:19.550
The notice for the interviews says

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:25.310
to come wearing casual clothing that 
you feel best expresses yourself.

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:31.440
Yes, sir, it does.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:33.730
But that's a trap.

00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:37.330
A diabolical pitfall.

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:40.810
For example, look at him.

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:44.790
No matter what the notice said,

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:47.110
he should have the common knowledge

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:49.740
that an interview at Teiai means 
a black suit, head to toe.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.010
It's an unwritten role.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:56.270
Every year, people unaware of the rule

00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:59.950
take that "casual dress" at face value 
and embarrass themselves.

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:04.470
They're not even worth interviewing.

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:07.590
They've already been eliminated.

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:15.970
<i>Tonegawa Yukio, the number two 
man of the massive Teiai Group.</i>

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.630
<i>He serves the monster 
of the financial sector.</i>

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:23.990
<i>This shot-caller rose to the position 
of President Hyoudou's right-hand man.</i>

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:28.820
<i>This is the story of the battles 
he waged as a middle manager,</i>

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:32.170
<i>in the shadows of the glory 
and fame he achieved...</i>

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:40.530
<i>The small, unremarkable story... about 
the struggles of a remarkable man.</i>

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:51.150
<b>Middle Management Blues</b>

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:51.150
<b><i>Mr. Tonegawa</i></b>

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:15.540
<i>The Teiai job interview, which determines 
the fate of all its applicants.</i>

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:15.540
<i>Agenda 09
</i>Cutlets

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:20.350
<i>The prospects are led to booths 
numbered one through ten,</i>

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:24.150
<i>and then in sequence, the interviews begin.</i>

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:28.530
Excuse me.

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:31.040
Please, have a seat.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:32.600
Thank you.

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:41.550
<i>The interviewers are one member of the 
executive staff and one man in black.</i>

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:46.800
<i>After a brief Q&A section, 
the interview concludes.</i>

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:49.640
Thank you for your time.

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:52.560
Have a safe trip home.

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:54.730
Thank you so much!

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:56.600
If you'll pardon me.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.980
<i>Those who have received this 
response are already...</i>

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:04.490
<i>Out! Rejected!</i>

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:07.780
<i>Those who are accepted...</i>

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:10.490
Thank you for coming in.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:15.750
You can go ahead and proceed 
through the door over there.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.400
<i>...are then guided.</i>

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:24.510
<i>Guided...</i>

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:28.040
<i>on their first step into the underworld!</i>

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:33.950
<b>Psst...</b>

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:57.780
Congratulations. Congratulations.

00:05:57.780 --> 00:06:01.550
Congratulations. Congratulations.

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:01.310
<b>Psst...</b>

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:04.050
<i>Once you're in Teiai, there's no escape.</i>

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:08.470
<i>Not if they see you as valuable!</i>

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:11.470
<i>And then...</i>

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:13.220
Pardon me.

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:18.480
<i>The next applicant enters the Tonegawa booth!</i>

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:20.980
Well, to start,

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:24.360
could you tell us why you applied at Teiai?

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:28.280
Right! Well, the way your company 
has such a direct approach to financing,

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:31.990
yet finds a way to conduct business 
creating a compassionate corporate culture

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:34.990
by making allowances and 
offering debtors a second chance,

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:36.620
<i>He's the real deal...</i>

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:39.510
convinced me to consider it one of the 
greatest financial institutions in the world!

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:39.870
<i>He has such passion for Teiai!</i>

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:42.510
And because I wanted to be a part of that,

00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:46.280
I applied for a position in the 
hopes of being able to work here!

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:48.390
All right, moving on...

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:53.140
<i>His education, his written submission, 
and his answers have been pretty good, too.</i>

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:56.090
<i>He's bound to get hired.</i>

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:59.480
Well, thank you for your time.

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:02.900
Have a safe trip home.

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:06.650
Thanks for your consideration! 
If you'll excuse me.

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:15.510
Tonegawa-sensei...

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:18.530
Surprised, Yamazaki?

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:24.050
It's true, he did have a love for Teiai,

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:27.210
but that's exactly why he's a bad choice.

00:07:28.810 --> 00:07:33.460
He called Teiai a wonderful business. 
That in itself proves...

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:37.110
he's off-mark! Fundamentally!

00:07:39.460 --> 00:07:43.850
Teiai is the dark side. 
Blacker than the blackest black.

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:45.610
Th-That's true...

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:49.110
His passion was forthright, 
but his actual perceptiveness...

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:52.390
If he can't even realize 
Teiai's true, dark nature,

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:54.730
he wouldn't last long here, would he?

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:58.500
Exactly. See, you do understand.

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:02.370
Okay, you handle the next one, Yamazaki.

00:08:02.930 --> 00:08:03.860
It's your call.

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:05.870
Me, sir?!

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:07.630
You're part of the core staff now.

00:08:08.110 --> 00:08:11.210
Dabbling with this kind of thing 
won't be a bad experience.

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:13.800
I understand.

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:17.510
C-Come on in.

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:19.670
Pardon me.

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:27.490
That face... Where have I...

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:31.650
<b>Hagio Kouichi</b>

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:34.400
D-Don't tell me you're...

00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:37.160
That's right.

00:08:37.810 --> 00:08:41.330
Thank you for taking good care 
of my brother, Tonegawa-sensei!

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:46.290
You're Ogio's brother?!

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:48.790
Er, no...

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:51.800
It's Hagio, sir, not Ogio.

00:08:56.170 --> 00:08:59.300
You look just like him. 
You even correct me the same way.

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:03.560
<i>This atmosphere is a good sign for him.</i>

00:09:03.970 --> 00:09:07.460
<i>Regardless of how it's done, 
the core of an interview</i>

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:10.900
<i>is managing to make the person 
doing the interview like you.</i>

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:13.140
<i>No, wait...</i>

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:14.550
<b>Psst...</b>

00:09:14.930 --> 00:09:17.320
<i>The vaguest sense of dissonance tickles him.</i>

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:19.380
Well, Yamazaki?

00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:20.250
Right.

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:24.020
W-Well...

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:27.240
<i>Yamazaki catches on!</i>

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:29.040
Thank you for your time.

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:31.710
Have a safe trip home.

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:33.150
Right!

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:37.610
I'll work hard to be as much use 
to Tonegawa-sensei as my brother!

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:49.250
You made the right call. I'm impressed.

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:50.980
Well, sir...

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:56.340
Did we really need any more...

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:57.490
Ogino

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:57.490
Hagio

00:09:56.340 --> 00:09:57.490
Hagio (Younger)

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:01.740
people whose names are too 
similar or look too much alike?

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:06.000
Precisely! Very shrewd, Yamazaki.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.490
Thank you, sir.

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:12.470
Yes, please come in.

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:15.510
Excuse me.

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:21.280
<b>Psst...</b>

00:10:21.990 --> 00:10:26.070
Well, if you could start by telling 
us why you applied to our company...

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:27.760
Certainly.

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:30.650
I find your vigorous approach to collections

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:34.050
and your ruthless, 
diabolical treatment of creditors

00:10:34.050 --> 00:10:38.830
to be exactly the kind of 
spartan corporate culture

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:42.660
that is necessary to 
survive in modern society.

00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:42.660
Tonegawa-sensei...

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:46.410
Look at this! His résumé is incredible!

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:48.910
And his responses have been great,

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:51.920
plus he got a perfect score on 
every part of the written exam!

00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:53.590
This man...

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:55.590
is a rare find!

00:10:57.340 --> 00:11:00.090
And more than anything else...

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:03.210
Look at his incredibly unique features!

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:08.500
With that face, there's no way you'd 
mix him up with the other men in black!

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:11.600
He's perfect.

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:14.410
I can't see a single flaw. He's hired!

00:11:14.410 --> 00:11:16.360
W-Wait... the thing is...

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:18.680
Thank you for coming in.

00:11:18.680 --> 00:11:20.520
If you'd just proceed through that—

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:21.860
Yamazaki, wait a minute!

00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:27.910
P-Please have a safe trip home.

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:37.050
Well, I hope to see you both 
at the entrance ceremony.

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:40.970
Tonegawa-sensei, why?

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:48.350
It's true, that applicant was on another 
level from the average man in black.

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:51.100
But... that's exactly the problem.

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:56.110
He stands out! He can't help but stand out, 
even more than the president!

00:11:57.650 --> 00:12:01.110
While the indistinct look of the 
usual men in black is a problem,

00:12:01.670 --> 00:12:03.780
the opposite extreme is just as bad!

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:07.460
Th-This is complicated! So complicated!

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:12.950
I had no idea that passing the 
Teiai interview was this difficult!

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:17.790
<b>Black Hole</b>

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:17.790
<i>Like escaping a black hole!</i>

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:22.550
<i>And so, the interviews continued 
without any major issues,</i>

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:25.550
<i>coming to a succesful conclusion!</i>

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:30.810
<i>The new hires at Teiai this year</i>

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:32.610
<i>number 25 in total!</i>

00:12:33.050 --> 00:12:37.810
Okay, could you give me 
more natural-looking smiles?

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:44.610
I'll see you next time.

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:56.880
<i>The afternoon break I've 
been waiting for all day...</i>

00:12:57.530 --> 00:13:00.880
<i>Tonegawa begins his lunch time!</i>

00:13:01.410 --> 00:13:05.190
<i>The fleeting moment of grace 
that a salaryman has to relax.</i>

00:13:05.190 --> 00:13:07.240
<i>Our moment of peace.</i>

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:12.890
<b>Hand-Made Soba Noodles</b>

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:12.890
<b>Sobahei</b>

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:12.890
<i>Normally I go for soba 
or the daily special,</i>

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:14.230
<i>but today...</i>

00:13:19.720 --> 00:13:22.150
<i>I'm exceptionally hungry.</i>

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:30.280
<b>The Cutlet Bog</b>

00:13:27.220 --> 00:13:30.280
<i>I'd normally never dine 
at a place like this,</i>

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:30.280
<b>Voluminous
Pork Cutlets!</b>

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:33.290
<i>but I'll give it a shot today</i>

00:13:33.640 --> 00:13:34.930
<i>and get my fill!</i>

00:13:36.180 --> 00:13:37.830
Here you go.

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:40.850
Welcome!

00:13:41.780 --> 00:13:43.130
Table for one, sir?

00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:46.170
Right this way, then.

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:56.890
<i>Well, that is a good amount 
of pork, I suppose...</i>

00:13:56.890 --> 00:13:59.150
<i>But overall, the serving is pretty typical.</i>

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:02.900
<i>Not enough to satisfy me at the moment.</i>

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:05.230
Is it all right if I order now?

00:14:05.230 --> 00:14:07.700
Sure! What would you like?

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:11.700
Give me the pork cutlet bowl. 
A large serving.

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:15.700
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:19.090
S-Sir... Are you sure about that?

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:23.800
What? You think it's too much for me?

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:25.960
No, I didn't mean...

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:30.690
Just bring the large serving 
already. No nitpicking.

00:14:30.690 --> 00:14:33.410
O-Okay. One large serving!

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:37.480
<b>Cutlet Bog</b>

00:14:35.620 --> 00:14:37.480
<i>And so, minutes later...</i>

00:14:37.880 --> 00:14:39.640
Here you go, sir.

00:14:41.430 --> 00:14:43.230
Your large pork cutlet bowl!

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:49.240
<i>Wh-What is this... 
overwhelming volume of food?!</i>

00:14:50.020 --> 00:14:51.990
<i>Is that a normal?</i>

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:53.870
<i>And this is a large?!</i>

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:57.620
<i>That's insane! Shouldn't there be more steps?!</i>

00:14:57.930 --> 00:15:00.570
<i>More steps between the sizes?!</i>

00:14:58.410 --> 00:15:03.130
<b>Normal</b>

00:14:59.890 --> 00:15:03.130
<b>Medium</b>

00:15:00.890 --> 00:15:03.130
<b>Large</b>

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:03.130
<b>Special</b>

00:15:04.470 --> 00:15:06.380
<i>Wait, no!</i>

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:10.880
<b>Menu</b>

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:10.880
<i>It actually does have steps...</i>

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:13.890
Pork Cutlet Bowls

00:15:11.290 --> 00:15:13.890
<i>But only from the normal size down!</i>

00:15:13.890 --> 00:15:17.890
<i>In other words, that isn't 
the normal helping...</i>

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:20.190
<i>Fool!</i>

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:25.940
<i>Why would someone your size 
order the ladies portion?!</i>

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:27.690
Excuse me...

00:15:28.790 --> 00:15:32.950
We usually ask people taking on the large 
size if they'd like to be photographed.

00:15:33.290 --> 00:15:35.300
Is it all right if we get a picture later?

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:37.460
Uh... a picture?

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:39.830
See up there?

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:43.480
<b>Too much, even for sumo wrestlers!</b>

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:46.710
<b>Professional Eater Jumbo Kuroda, Defeated</b>

00:15:42.490 --> 00:15:45.830
<i>Lined up one after another 
is a history of defeat!</i>

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:46.710
<b>Tokyo Rugby Club, defeated...!</b>

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:52.720
See, the thing is, no one's ever 
been able to finish it before.

00:15:52.720 --> 00:16:00.980
<b>Teiai Finance defeated!
I was wrong! -Tonegawa</b>

00:15:56.820 --> 00:16:00.980
<i>And now, a new page is about to 
be written in that history book!</i>

00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:03.350
I-Inconceivable!

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:07.530
W-Wait a second!

00:16:07.530 --> 00:16:09.650
Having second thoughts?

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:14.160
B-But... I...

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:19.190
Just bring the large serving 
already. No nitpicking.

00:16:20.420 --> 00:16:24.710
<i>After I said all that, I can't back down!</i>

00:16:25.190 --> 00:16:29.120
<i>So much for my peaceful lunch time... Why?</i>

00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:31.080
<i>Why did this happen?!</i>

00:16:35.110 --> 00:16:36.390
Get that camera ready.

00:16:37.730 --> 00:16:40.060
You're going to witness a legend.

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:42.390
You'll have but an instant to snap the shutter.

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:52.600
<i>Tonegawa steels himself!</i>

00:17:07.300 --> 00:17:11.860
<i>He dives into the pork cutlet sea 
like his life depends on it!</i>

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:16.010
Got it!

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:29.590
<i>Good. That takes care of the pork.</i>

00:17:29.590 --> 00:17:31.270
<i>That just leaves the rice...</i>

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:38.400
<i>I-It can't be!</i>

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:41.000
<i>Amid the grains, another cutlet lies in wait!</i>

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:43.540
<i>Tonegawa miscalculated!</i>

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:57.470
<i>What he thought was a double 
layer was, in fact, a triple!</i>

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:03.350
<i>A bona fide katsu-dungeon!</i>

00:18:05.240 --> 00:18:09.630
<i>He is rocked on all sides 
by wild waves of pork!</i>

00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:12.610
<i>It takes the form of a giant beast,</i>

00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:16.020
<i>ready to swallow Tonegawa instead!</i>

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:23.620
<i>It's eat or be eaten! A clash of 
wills with survival on the line!</i>

00:18:26.660 --> 00:18:30.880
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:18:33.330 --> 00:18:37.560
M-Maybe you should give up now...

00:18:37.560 --> 00:18:38.760
Give up?

00:18:40.020 --> 00:18:42.890
There's no such thing, not if you're serious.

00:18:44.710 --> 00:18:47.640
And playtime is over!

00:18:57.280 --> 00:18:59.780
You can't dream about 
how nice it'd be to win!

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:02.780
In life, you have to win!

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:15.590
<i>Tonegawa finishes the bowl!</i>

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:18.620
Amazing! He actually finished it!

00:19:18.620 --> 00:19:20.720
Congratulations, sir!

00:19:22.340 --> 00:19:26.470
Sorry, could you give me 
a more natural smile?

00:19:30.530 --> 00:19:35.060
Hey... Isn't Tonegawa-sensei's 
lunch taking a little too long?

00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:36.990
Now that you mention it...

00:19:36.990 --> 00:19:39.820
It's almost time for the afternoon meeting.

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:41.930
I wonder if something happened.

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:45.750
Oh, Tonegawa-sensei.

00:19:46.850 --> 00:19:48.190
Where were you, sir?

00:19:48.190 --> 00:19:49.910
We were getting worried!

00:19:50.520 --> 00:19:51.920
Stay away from me!

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:56.150
I'm not responsible for what could 
happen if you touch me right now.

00:19:59.370 --> 00:20:02.650
Let's get the afternoon meeting started.

00:20:02.650 --> 00:20:07.310
<i>What... What the hell happened 
to him during his lunch?</i>

00:20:18.370 --> 00:20:20.940
It's Tonegawa, sir. You called for me?

00:20:22.870 --> 00:20:25.250
There you are, Tonegawa.

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:29.870
What do you think of these cutlet sandwiches?

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:29.870
<b>Cutlet Sandwich</b>

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:38.460
You should eat some.

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:47.470
<i>Once again, the sea of pork cutlets rages. 
A nightmare that never ends!</i>

00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:55.830
<i>Hang in there, Tonegawa. 
Don't give up, Tonegawa.</i>

00:20:57.050 --> 00:21:01.310
<i>This is the story of a lone man who 
struggles between his employer</i>

00:21:01.310 --> 00:21:05.490
<i>and his own employees, the men in black...</i>

00:21:05.830 --> 00:21:10.240
<i>Tonegawa Yukio: Middle Manager!</i>

00:21:14.170 --> 00:21:15.460
<i>In a word...</i>

00:21:16.360 --> 00:21:18.230
<i>sandwiched.</i>

00:22:54.730 --> 00:22:56.950
Next time: "Rehearsal"!

00:22:55.790 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>Rehearsal</b>
